he only way to salvation from suffering  this pessimistic outlook towards life is  observed all over his narrative and it  was because of this tone that many refer  to him as the philosopher of pessimism  the absurdity of reality has always been  the main area of interest for most  Western philosophers Schopenhauer in his  attempt to create meaning out of this  absurdity illuminated a very pessimistic  rhetoric take for example the following  passage from the world as will and  representation into this world to this  scene of tormented and agonized beings  who only continue to exist by devouring  each other  in which therefore every ravenous beast  is the living grave of thousands of  others and it's self maintenance is a  chain of painful deaths and in which the  capacity for filling pain increases with  knowledge and therefore reaches its  highest degree in man a degree which is  the higher the more intelligent the man  is to this world it has been so to apply  the system of optimism and demonstrate  to us that it is the best of all  possible worlds the absurdity is  clearing it is self-evident that he's in  her world is tormented you to the  absurdity that it's prevalent all over  our existence this nihilistic approach  connotes an alignment with the idea of  determinism deuteron ability to  influence the wheel however he doesn't  give up he understands that there is an  escape even if this can be found on a  metaphysical level not merely that the  world exists but still more that it is  such a miserable and melancholy world is  that romantic problem of metaphysics  here he is tapping into the world of  metaphysics by realizing that there  needs to be another dimension to our  existence one we will never experience  if we keep recycling the same thinking  modus ad infinitum the life of every  individual viewed as a whole and in  general and when only its most  significant features are emphasized is  really tragedy but gone through in  detail it has the character 